config BR2_PACKAGE_IIO_WS
	bool "iio_ws"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBIIO
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBWEBSOCKETS
	help
	  IIO stream to WebSocket Proxy

	  iio_ws_proxy.c links directly against -liio and -lwebsockets
	  (see app/iio_ws/Makefile) but this Config.in never declared
	  either as a real Buildroot dependency. It "worked" only by
	  accident: every board building this so far also happened to
	  pull in BR2_PACKAGE_LIBIIO itself and, separately,
	  BR2_PACKAGE_LIBWEBSOCKETS via tezuka_tools_mini's own select
	  list (a mosquitto-websockets leftover, unrelated to this
	  package -- see that Config.in's comment). Removing that
	  leftover select exposed this: "fatal error: libwebsockets.h:
	  No such file or directory" building fishball_mini{,_7020} in
	  CI run 35263057480. Declaring both selects here, where the
	  real dependency actually lives, fixes it properly instead of
	  restoring the accidental one.

